1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,731
Italy, as a country, is only 165
years old. So who built Rome?

2
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:09,091
Legend says Rome was
founded in 753 BC,

3
00:00:09,131 --> 00:00:12,139
on seven hills
beside the Tiber.

4
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:14,679
By the year 80, Rome
rules the Mediterranean,

5
00:00:14,719 --> 00:00:17,860
and the Colosseum
opens its gates.

6
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,940
In 476, the last
Western emperor falls,

7
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:23,097
and Italy breaks apart.

8
00:00:23,137 --> 00:00:25,717
In the 1400s, Florence
sparks the Renaissance,

9
00:00:25,757 --> 00:00:28,750
with Leonardo
and Michelangelo.

10
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:31,890
In 1610, Galileo points
his telescope at Jupiter,

11
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:34,321
and finds four moons.

12
00:00:34,361 --> 00:00:37,401
In 1861, the many
states finally unite

13
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:39,685
as one Kingdom of Italy.

14
00:00:39,725 --> 00:00:42,785
In 1946, Italians
vote for a republic,

15
00:00:42,825 --> 00:00:45,180
and scooters
fill the streets.

16
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,940
Today, about 59 million
people live here,

17
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:51,623
with more World Heritage
Sites than any other country.

18
00:00:51,663 --> 00:00:55,440
Where should we print
next? Tell us below.

